<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baji Rao II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1851">1851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baji Rao II was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> from 1795 to 1818. Driven out by Yashwantrao Holkar, he accepted British protection in the Treaty of Bassein in 1802, which helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-maratha-war">Second Anglo-Maratha War</a>. He rose against the British in 1817, was defeated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-maratha-war">Third Anglo-Maratha War</a> and surrendered in 1818, after which the office of Peshwa was abolished and he lived on a pension at Bithur until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baji-rao-ii.jpg" alt="Baji Rao II" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dhakate_Bajirava_Saheb._Coloured_lithograph,_1888._Wellcome_V0045040.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
